  "seeds": "train_seed for random, numpy and TensorFlow (weight initialisation, augmentation, batch order); no split seed: the folds and the samples are deterministic",
  "device": "CPU"
 },
 "sequence": "phase 1, for each of the 12 positions in order: the fitting and dev frames of the unit assembled and their keys checked against the card of the accepted run; the training (pad_anet_comparison.anet_trainer, the model built with the registry); rule (n) on the history and on the restored weights; the in-memory dev scored; the checkpoint saved; the card; the dev scored with the saved checkpoint (nuaa_folds_run.tf_scorer), its logits and the val_loss checked against the card. Phase 2, after the 12 trainings, for each evaluable model: the checkpoint reloaded and checked against the registry; the ordinary dev; the BN statistics re-estimated on its fitting set (copy in memory); the consistency pass; the re-estimated dev; the checks of PR #27; the agreement with the phase-1 scores; thresholds, decisions and counts of both BN states. The sequence of pad_arch_run (C2) with the AttackNet trainer, the registry and rule (n)",
 "non_evaluable": {
  "rule": "rule (n) of the pre-registration (PROTOCOL.md \u00a76 (k)/(n), pad_anet_definitions.training_outcome): a non-finite value in the history does not stop the run; the quantity and the first non-finite epoch are recorded; the restored epoch is that of the smallest finite val_loss; without a finite val_loss, or with non-finite restored weights, the model is not evaluable: no checkpoint, no phase 2",
  "in_memory_dev": "before the checkpoint is saved, the dev and the fitting are scored with the model in memory in the ordinary state (pad_anet_comparison.forward_checked, inference only: no state of the model, no seed and no recorded epoch time changes): non-finite scores or logits make the model not evaluable, without checkpoint",
  "fitting_scores": "the fitting is scored in both BN states: in the ordinary state by the in-memory pass of phase 1 (non_evaluable.in_memory_dev), in the re-estimated state by the consistency pass of phase 2; non-finite scores or logits there, or on the dev in either BN state, make the model not evaluable",
  "statistics": "non-finite re-estimated statistics (the message of nuaa_bn_recalibration) make the model not evaluable, before any output of its phase 2 is written",
  "record": "a not evaluable model keeps its card in restricted/; a model found not evaluable in phase 2 keeps its checkpoint and phase-1 dev scores in restricted/, marked not evaluable in models.csv, and the evaluation does not score it on the test (amended PROTOCOL.md \u00a76 (k)/(n)); models.csv, summary.json and report.md give the status 'not evaluable' with the reason; it does not change the outcome of the run; no new attempt with the same seed for it"
 },
 "after_stop": "a choice of the author, recorded in the amended PROTOCOL.md \u00a76 (k)/(n) of this delivery, which replaces the pre-registered sentence 'resumed only for the missing trainings': a run stopped at its cap, by SIGUSR1, by a FAIL, a MISMATCH or an interruption is not resumed within its folder; it keeps its folder and outcome and, after its outcome has been reported on the C5 card, is repeated as a new attempt in a new folder from position 1, with the same seeds, code and configuration, before the evaluation, as in C2; the repetition retrains every position, those not evaluable included, and their outcome in the last attempt is the one evaluated; a run is never repeated because of a not evaluable model; the evaluation reads, for each of the six runs, only the last attempt, which must be PASS, with phase 1 complete for the 12 positions (not evaluable models included)",
